description:
Discovery Source: kiro-enhancement branch - Kiro CLI argument workaround
Discovered During: serve phase

Impact:
plugins/kiro/README.md line 81 shows @line-cook lc-042 as a valid example in the "@Prompt Invocation" Examples section. This directly contradicts the Known Issues section below it that says arguments are discarded.

Context:
Replace with no-arg example and add a note about natural language for arguments:
  @line-prep
  @line-cook
  @line-run
> Note: To pass arguments, use natural language: say "cook lc-042" instead of @line-cook lc-042. See Known Issues.
